WEBVTT

1
00:01:51.360 --> 00:01:53.760
HIGH SEPTON: May the Warrior
grant him courage

2
00:01:53.920 --> 00:01:56.800
and protect him in these perilous times.

3
00:01:56.960 --> 00:01:58.800
May the Smith grant him strength

4
00:01:58.960 --> 00:02:01.280
that he might bear this heavy burden

5
00:02:01.440 --> 00:02:02.840
and may the Crone.

6
00:02:03.000 --> 00:02:05.600
she that knows the fate of all men.

7
00:02:05.760 --> 00:02:07.760
show him the path he must walk

8
00:02:07.920 --> 00:02:11.600
and guide him through the dark places
that lie ahead.

9
00:02:11.760 --> 00:02:13.680
In the light of the Seven.
I now proclaim

10
00:02:13.840 --> 00:02:17.120
Tommen of the House Baratheon
First of His Name

11
00:02:17.280 --> 00:02:19.720
King of the Andals and the First Men

12
00:02:19.880 --> 00:02:22.760
and Lord of the Seven Kingdoms.

13
00:02:25.880 --> 00:02:27.240
Long may he reign!

14
00:02:27.400 --> 00:02:29.080
ALL: Long may he reign!

15
00:02:29.240 --> 00:02:32.080
(CHEERING)

16
00:02:39.400 --> 00:02:41.080
Special day.

17
00:02:48.160 --> 00:02:51.080
(CROWD CHATTING)

18
00:02:58.800 --> 00:03:00.320
Your Grace.

19
00:03:02.280 --> 00:03:04.040
Your Grace.

20
00:03:27.080 --> 00:03:29.160
-Your Grace.
-Your Grace.

21
00:03:44.080 --> 00:03:45.760
Your Grace.

22
00:03:48.840 --> 00:03:50.440
There he is.

23
00:03:51.480 --> 00:03:52.840
Long may he reign.

24
00:03:53.000 --> 00:03:54.400
Long may he reign.

25
00:03:58.240 --> 00:04:00.880
He sits the throne
like he was born to it.

26
00:04:01.040 --> 00:04:04.320
Yes. He wasn't. though. was he?

27
00:04:05.400 --> 00:04:07.240
No. he wasn't.

28
00:04:12.320 --> 00:04:14.440
You still mourn for Joffrey?

29
00:04:14.600 --> 00:04:16.280
He was my husband. My king.

30
00:04:16.440 --> 00:04:18.640
He would have been your nightmare.

31
00:04:22.280 --> 00:04:24.200
Your Grace. I feel--

32
00:04:24.360 --> 00:04:28.280
You knew exactly what he was.
I did. too.

33
00:04:28.440 --> 00:04:33.040
You never love anything in the world
the way you love your first child.

34
00:04:34.840 --> 00:04:36.760
Doesn't matter what they do.

35
00:04:39.680 --> 00:04:42.240
And what he did. it shocked me.

36
00:04:44.560 --> 00:04:47.440
-Do you think I'm easily shocked?
-No.

37
00:04:47.600 --> 00:04:50.880
The things he did shocked me.

38
00:04:57.480 --> 00:04:59.080
He's only a boy.

39
00:04:59.240 --> 00:05:01.160
A good boy. A decent boy.

40
00:05:01.320 --> 00:05:03.400
He always has been.

41
00:05:03.560 --> 00:05:06.120
Who was the last decent king. I wonder?

42
00:05:06.280 --> 00:05:08.920
He could be the first man
who sits on that throne in 50 years

43
00:05:09.080 --> 00:05:11.160
to actually deserve it.

44
00:05:12.480 --> 00:05:15.320
It would be some consolation.
wouldn't it?

45
00:05:15.480 --> 00:05:17.640
For all the horror that put him there.

46
00:05:22.880 --> 00:05:24.880
He will need help...

47
00:05:26.160 --> 00:05:28.040
if he's going to rule well.

48
00:05:28.200 --> 00:05:30.080
He has you.

49
00:05:30.240 --> 00:05:32.200
A mother is not enough.

50
00:05:34.160 --> 00:05:36.800
You're still interested in being queen.
I take it?

51
00:05:36.960 --> 00:05:38.760
(SCOFFS)

52
00:05:38.920 --> 00:05:40.440
After all that's happened--

53
00:05:43.600 --> 00:05:46.480
it sounds strange. I know. but I. uh--

54
00:05:46.640 --> 00:05:48.960
I haven't even given any thought to it.

55
00:05:49.120 --> 00:05:50.520
what comes next.

56
00:05:50.680 --> 00:05:53.400
It would be a great honor. of course.

57
00:05:53.560 --> 00:05:56.960
But I will have to speak to my father
about it.

58
00:05:58.240 --> 00:06:01.880
Yes. speak to your father.

59
00:06:02.040 --> 00:06:03.800
I'll speak to mine.

60
00:06:08.120 --> 00:06:11.040
We may be faced with an alarming number
of weddings soon.

61
00:06:11.200 --> 00:06:13.200
(CHUCKLES)

62
00:06:13.360 --> 00:06:16.080
I won't even know what to call you.

63
00:06:16.240 --> 00:06:19.520
Sister?
(SIGHS)

64
00:06:19.680 --> 00:06:21.920
Or Mother?

65
00:06:22.080 --> 00:06:23.520
(SCOFFS)

66
00:06:24.880 --> 00:06:27.240
King Joffrey Baratheon is dead.

67
00:06:29.360 --> 00:06:30.800
Murdered at his own wedding.

68
00:06:30.960 --> 00:06:34.000
BARRISTAN: And we have taken
the Meereenese navy. Your Grace.

69
00:06:34.160 --> 00:06:36.040
The Second Sons
took the Meereenese navy.

70
00:06:36.200 --> 00:06:40.640
-Who told you to take the navy?
-No one.

71
00:06:40.800 --> 00:06:42.560
So why did you do it?

72
00:06:42.720 --> 00:06:44.680
I heard you liked ships.

73
00:06:48.400 --> 00:06:51.240
-How many ships?
-93. Your Grace.

74
00:06:51.400 --> 00:06:55.240
-How many men can they carry?
-9.300. not counting sailors.

75
00:06:55.400 --> 00:06:57.680
Would that be enough
to take King's Landing?

76
00:06:57.840 --> 00:06:59.160
The Lannisters have more.

77
00:06:59.320 --> 00:07:01.320
BARRISTAN: They've been fighting
Joffrey's wars for years.

78
00:07:01.480 --> 00:07:03.160
They're tired. dispersed.

79
00:07:03.320 --> 00:07:05.280
And now their king is dead.

80
00:07:05.440 --> 00:07:09.400
8.000 Unsullied. 2.000 Second Sons

81
00:07:09.560 --> 00:07:11.440
sailing into Blackwater Bay

82
00:07:11.600 --> 00:07:13.960
and storming the gates without warning.

83
00:07:17.160 --> 00:07:19.440
It's hard to say. It could be enough.

84
00:07:19.600 --> 00:07:22.640
But we're not fighting to make you
queen of King's Landing.

85
00:07:22.800 --> 00:07:25.000
10.000 men can't conquer Westeros.

86
00:07:25.160 --> 00:07:27.160
The old houses will flock to our queen

87
00:07:27.320 --> 00:07:28.680
when she crosses the Narrow Sea.

88
00:07:28.840 --> 00:07:31.320
The old houses will flock
to whichever side they think will win.

89
00:07:31.480 --> 00:07:33.440
as they always have.

90
00:07:35.920 --> 00:07:37.800
There's other news.

91
00:07:37.960 --> 00:07:39.680
From Yunkai.

92
00:07:39.840 --> 00:07:42.520
Without the Unsullied
to enforce your rule.

93
00:07:42.680 --> 00:07:45.720
the Wise Masters
have retaken control of the city.

94
00:07:45.880 --> 00:07:48.320
They've reenslaved
the freedmen who stayed behind

95
00:07:48.480 --> 00:07:51.800
and sworn to take revenge against you.

96
00:07:51.960 --> 00:07:53.800
And in Astapor.

97
00:07:53.960 --> 00:07:56.240
the council you installed
to rule over the city

98
00:07:56.400 --> 00:07:59.400
has been overthrown
by a butcher named Cleon

99
00:07:59.560 --> 00:08:02.840
who's declared himself
"His Imperial Majesty."

100
00:08:04.880 --> 00:08:06.680
Please leave me.

101
00:08:11.560 --> 00:08:13.400
Not you. Jorah.

102
00:08:25.600 --> 00:08:27.640
It appears my liberation of Slaver's Bay

103
00:08:27.800 --> 00:08:29.520
isn't going quite as planned.

104
00:08:31.600 --> 00:08:33.600
You could sail for Westeros

105
00:08:33.760 --> 00:08:35.400
and leave it all behind.

106
00:08:35.560 --> 00:08:37.000
A boy sits on the Iron Throne.

107
00:08:37.160 --> 00:08:41.320
A boy many believe
to be a bastard with no right to it.

108
00:08:41.480 --> 00:08:43.560
They've never been more vulnerable.

109
00:08:43.720 --> 00:08:46.240
You counseled me against rashness
once in Qarth.

110
00:08:46.400 --> 00:08:48.720
I didn't listen.

111
00:08:48.880 --> 00:08:50.800
That all worked out well.

112
00:08:50.960 --> 00:08:53.800
(CHUCKLES)

113
00:08:57.960 --> 00:09:00.160
How can I rule seven kingdoms

114
00:09:00.320 --> 00:09:03.840
if I can't control Slaver's Bay?

115
00:09:04.000 --> 00:09:06.600
Why should anyone trust me?

116
00:09:06.760 --> 00:09:09.080
Why should anyone follow me?

117
00:09:09.240 --> 00:09:10.600
You're a Targaryen.

118
00:09:10.760 --> 00:09:12.920
You're the Mother of Dragons.

119
00:09:14.800 --> 00:09:16.840
I need to be more than that.

120
00:09:23.440 --> 00:09:28.440
I will not let those I have freed
slide back into chains.

121
00:09:28.600 --> 00:09:30.400
I will not sail for Westeros.

122
00:09:30.560 --> 00:09:32.320
What. then?

123
00:09:33.800 --> 00:09:35.880
I will do what queens do.

124
00:09:39.520 --> 00:09:41.240
I will rule.

125
00:10:15.400 --> 00:10:17.240
Pull up your hood.

126
00:10:19.160 --> 00:10:21.120
A memorable shade.

127
00:10:22.280 --> 00:10:23.960
But how would they know?

128
00:10:24.120 --> 00:10:27.600
You know what kind of stories
poor men enjoy the most?

129
00:10:27.760 --> 00:10:30.200
Ones about rich girls
they'll never meet.

130
00:10:34.600 --> 00:10:36.840
Is this the only way into the Eyrie?

131
00:10:37.000 --> 00:10:38.840
The mountains are impassable.

132
00:10:39.000 --> 00:10:42.160
If you want to get to the Eyrie.
you need to go through the Bloody Gate.

133
00:10:43.360 --> 00:10:45.560
It doesn't matter
how large your army is.

134
00:10:45.720 --> 00:10:48.200
if you attack this gate.
you do it on this road.

135
00:10:48.360 --> 00:10:50.200
three men abreast

136
00:10:50.360 --> 00:10:52.760
and get slaughtered like goats.

137
00:10:53.920 --> 00:10:55.520
The first Lords of the Vale
didn't have much.

138
00:10:55.680 --> 00:10:57.000
but they had these mountains

139
00:10:57.160 --> 00:10:59.200
and they knew how to use them.

140
00:10:59.360 --> 00:11:01.040
And the fortress they built here
has never been overcome.

141
00:11:01.200 --> 00:11:04.720
Not once in 1.000 years.

142
00:11:04.880 --> 00:11:07.440
Know your strengths. use them wisely.

143
00:11:07.600 --> 00:11:10.640
and one man can be worth 10.000.

144
00:11:15.200 --> 00:11:16.880
KNIGHT: Who would pass the Bloody Gate?

145
00:11:17.040 --> 00:11:19.800
Lord Petyr Baelish and his niece Alayne.

146
00:11:24.520 --> 00:11:27.880
-Stand to.
-Stand to!

147
00:11:29.640 --> 00:11:32.280
Welcome back. Lord Baelish.

148
00:11:32.440 --> 00:11:34.920
(GATE CLANKING)

149
00:11:57.040 --> 00:12:00.600
(DOOR OPENS)

150
00:12:00.760 --> 00:12:02.800
Uncle Petyr!

151
00:12:04.280 --> 00:12:06.080
LITTLEFINGER: My lord.

152
00:12:12.160 --> 00:12:14.120
Oh.

153
00:12:14.280 --> 00:12:18.120
I have brought you a gift.

154
00:12:22.280 --> 00:12:24.480
-Lord Baelish.
-My lady.

155
00:12:24.640 --> 00:12:28.680
-Look what Uncle Petyr brought me.
-A beautiful gift for a beautiful boy.

156
00:12:28.840 --> 00:12:31.840
It's a pleasure to make
your acquaintance. Lady Arryn.

157
00:12:32.000 --> 00:12:35.760
-My name is Al--
-Oh. do take down that hood. child.

158
00:12:35.920 --> 00:12:38.360
Don't you think know who you are?

159
00:12:38.520 --> 00:12:42.120
You think I'd let my intended
leave the Eyrie on urgent business

160
00:12:42.280 --> 00:12:44.760
without knowing what that business was?

161
00:12:45.880 --> 00:12:50.440
I let him go so he could bring you
here to me.

162
00:12:53.360 --> 00:12:55.600
My flesh and blood.

163
00:12:57.480 --> 00:12:59.240
It's wonderful to meet you. Aunt Lysa.

164
00:12:59.400 --> 00:13:01.280
You mustn't call me that
in front of anyone else.

165
00:13:01.440 --> 00:13:04.040
-Of course. I understand.
-No one can know you're here.

166
00:13:04.200 --> 00:13:06.240
It would put us
in a very precarious position.

167
00:13:06.400 --> 00:13:07.760
I would never say a thing.

168
00:13:07.920 --> 00:13:09.880
The Lannisters want to destroy us.

169
00:13:10.040 --> 00:13:12.120
They've been trying for years.

170
00:13:12.280 --> 00:13:14.040
Now they know what it feels like.

171
00:13:14.200 --> 00:13:19.360
Mummy said they killed your mother and
they chopped off your brother's head.

172
00:13:19.520 --> 00:13:22.640
They did. and my father's.

173
00:13:22.800 --> 00:13:26.320
They killed my father. too. with poison.
(SIGHS)

174
00:13:26.480 --> 00:13:29.560
I wanted to make
the little Lannister baby man fly.

175
00:13:29.720 --> 00:13:31.320
but Mother said I couldn't.

176
00:13:31.480 --> 00:13:33.160
Make him fly?

177
00:13:33.320 --> 00:13:34.960
Through the Moon Door.

178
00:13:38.040 --> 00:13:39.360
(GIGGLES)

179
00:13:39.520 --> 00:13:41.680
LYSA: And on top of everything else.

180
00:13:41.840 --> 00:13:44.000
they made you marry that filthy troll.

181
00:13:44.160 --> 00:13:47.480
They did. They made us both.
Lord Tyrion didn't want to.

182
00:13:47.640 --> 00:13:49.480
LYSA: I don't believe that for a moment.

183
00:13:49.640 --> 00:13:51.440
Did he force himself on you?

184
00:13:51.600 --> 00:13:54.040
No. We never--

185
00:13:54.200 --> 00:13:57.840
Good. Robin. this is your cousin Sansa.

186
00:13:58.000 --> 00:13:59.640
But you're not to call her Sansa
in front of anyone

187
00:13:59.800 --> 00:14:01.840
but Uncle Petyr and myself.
Do you understand?

188
00:14:02.000 --> 00:14:05.400
Sansa. this is my son Robin.

189
00:14:05.560 --> 00:14:07.160
It's a pleasure to meet you. Robin.

190
00:14:07.320 --> 00:14:09.200
Robin. show Sansa to her chamber.

191
00:14:09.360 --> 00:14:11.640
Take the back stairs.

192
00:14:14.080 --> 00:14:17.200
Go. We'll speak soon.

193
00:14:25.400 --> 00:14:26.920
What took you so long?

194
00:14:27.080 --> 00:14:29.680
Arranging for the ascension
of King Tommen I.

195
00:14:29.840 --> 00:14:33.080
extricating Sansa.
getting her here alive.

196
00:14:33.240 --> 00:14:38.000
She's here. We've spent more than enough
time on her for one evening.

197
00:14:38.160 --> 00:14:40.840
(SIGHS)
Let's get married tonight.

198
00:14:41.000 --> 00:14:43.600
Ought we not...

199
00:14:43.760 --> 00:14:46.080
inform the Lords of the Vale
about the ceremony?

200
00:14:46.240 --> 00:14:47.920
There's only one Lord of the Vale.

201
00:14:48.080 --> 00:14:49.640
The others can all hang.

202
00:14:49.800 --> 00:14:52.080
Lurking and simpering
on the stairs like buzzards

203
00:14:52.240 --> 00:14:55.160
the moment my husband died.
trying to get their claws in me.

204
00:14:55.320 --> 00:14:58.920
-I do think that we could wait until--
-I'm done waiting. Petyr.

205
00:14:59.080 --> 00:15:02.360
We had our wedding night many years ago.

206
00:15:02.520 --> 00:15:06.000
-Don't you remember?
-Like it was yesterday.

207
00:15:06.160 --> 00:15:10.440
What wife would do for you
the things I've done for you?

208
00:15:10.600 --> 00:15:13.240
What wife would trust you
the way I've trusted you?

209
00:15:13.400 --> 00:15:15.680
When you gave me those drops

210
00:15:15.840 --> 00:15:18.320
and told me to pour them
into Jon's wine.

211
00:15:18.480 --> 00:15:19.800
my husband's wine--

212
00:15:19.960 --> 00:15:22.880
when you told me
to write a letter to Cat

213
00:15:23.040 --> 00:15:26.080
telling her it was the Lannisters--

214
00:15:26.240 --> 00:15:29.440
(MOANS)

215
00:15:37.280 --> 00:15:38.680
The deed is done.

216
00:15:38.840 --> 00:15:41.800
Faded into nothing.

217
00:15:41.960 --> 00:15:44.040
Only speaking of it can make it real.

218
00:15:47.840 --> 00:15:53.120
Tonight it is. then.
(CHUCKLES)

219
00:15:53.280 --> 00:15:54.720
Let me bathe and dress for the occasion.

220
00:15:54.880 --> 00:15:58.400
Once I'm presentable.
I'll call on the septon immediately.

221
00:16:05.520 --> 00:16:07.800
I'm warning you.

222
00:16:07.960 --> 00:16:11.680
I'm going to scream
when my husband makes love to me.

223
00:16:11.840 --> 00:16:14.280
I'm going to scream so loud.

224
00:16:14.440 --> 00:16:17.360
they'll hear me
clear across the Narrow Sea.

225
00:16:19.880 --> 00:16:22.200
(LYSA SCREAMING)

226
00:16:23.920 --> 00:16:26.560
(GRUNTING. MOANING)

227
00:16:28.320 --> 00:16:30.360
(SCREAMING)

228
00:16:33.520 --> 00:16:36.840
(MOANING. SCREAMING CONTINUES)

229
00:16:41.000 --> 00:16:44.200
When will the wedding take place.
in your mind?

230
00:16:44.360 --> 00:16:46.040
As soon as decency permits.

231
00:16:46.200 --> 00:16:50.640
After we've allowed Tommen the
appropriate time to mourn his brother

232
00:16:50.800 --> 00:16:52.280
and Margaery to mourn her husband.

233
00:16:52.440 --> 00:16:55.440
-A fortnight?
-That seems reasonable.

234
00:16:55.600 --> 00:16:58.560
No jugglers. no jousting dwarves.

235
00:16:58.720 --> 00:17:00.840
no 77-course meals.

236
00:17:03.120 --> 00:17:05.040
And your wedding to Loras?

237
00:17:06.440 --> 00:17:07.760
Shortly after Tommen's.

238
00:17:07.920 --> 00:17:09.880
-Shortly?
-A fortnight.

239
00:17:11.680 --> 00:17:13.440
I know you don't like them.

240
00:17:13.600 --> 00:17:15.560
I didn't like your husband.

241
00:17:15.720 --> 00:17:19.280
Used to pat me on the back a lot.
I didn't trust him.

242
00:17:19.440 --> 00:17:21.200
We had that in common.

243
00:17:21.360 --> 00:17:25.760
You don't need to make formal alliances
with people you trust.

244
00:17:25.920 --> 00:17:28.600
Then whom can we trust?

245
00:17:28.760 --> 00:17:31.560
Ourselves alone.

246
00:17:33.640 --> 00:17:35.520
The Tyrells

247
00:17:35.680 --> 00:17:37.640
are our only true rivals

248
00:17:37.800 --> 00:17:39.520
in terms of resources

249
00:17:39.680 --> 00:17:42.600
and we need them on our side.

250
00:17:42.760 --> 00:17:45.400
Robert wasn't particularly rich.

251
00:17:45.560 --> 00:17:48.480
Robert had me funding him.

252
00:17:48.640 --> 00:17:51.160
Wars swallow gold
like a pit in the earth.

253
00:17:51.320 --> 00:17:54.680
I suppose that explains
why we did so well in the last one.

254
00:17:54.840 --> 00:17:58.320
Do you know how much gold was mined
in the Westerlands this past year?

255
00:17:58.480 --> 00:18:01.960
-Haven't a clue.
-Go on. your best guess.

256
00:18:02.120 --> 00:18:03.840
Pounds. tons. ounces?

257
00:18:04.000 --> 00:18:06.080
Doesn't matter. The answer is the same.

258
00:18:07.600 --> 00:18:10.560
-That can't be.
-Our last working mine ran dry

259
00:18:10.720 --> 00:18:12.840
three years ago.

260
00:18:13.000 --> 00:18:14.680
Then how do we pay for anything?

261
00:18:14.840 --> 00:18:16.880
The crown owes the Iron Bank of Braavos

262
00:18:17.040 --> 00:18:18.720
a tremendous amount of money.

263
00:18:18.880 --> 00:18:20.480
How much?

264
00:18:21.920 --> 00:18:23.560
A tremendous amount.

265
00:18:25.400 --> 00:18:28.280
There must be someone at the Iron Bank
you can speak to.

266
00:18:28.440 --> 00:18:31.160
-come to some arrangement.
-The Iron Bank is the Iron Bank.

267
00:18:31.320 --> 00:18:32.880
There is no someone.

268
00:18:33.040 --> 00:18:35.280
Someone does work there.
It is comprised of people.

269
00:18:35.440 --> 00:18:37.560
And a temple is comprised of stones.

270
00:18:37.720 --> 00:18:40.680
One stone crumbles
and another takes its place.

271
00:18:40.840 --> 00:18:44.920
And the temple holds its form
for 1.000 years or more.

272
00:18:45.080 --> 00:18:48.320
That's what the Iron Bank is-- a temple.

273
00:18:48.480 --> 00:18:52.840
We all live in its shadow
and almost none of us know it.

274
00:18:53.000 --> 00:18:54.880
You can't run from them.
You can't cheat them.

275
00:18:55.040 --> 00:18:58.160
You can't sway them with excuses.

276
00:18:58.320 --> 00:19:01.720
If you owe them money
and you don't want to crumble yourself.

277
00:19:01.880 --> 00:19:03.320
you pay it back.

278
00:19:03.480 --> 00:19:07.080
Vesting the Tyrells in the crown
will help a great deal in this respect.

279
00:19:07.240 --> 00:19:10.520
It's for the good of the family.
I understand that.

280
00:19:14.200 --> 00:19:16.800
I'm not sure my brothers do.

281
00:19:20.200 --> 00:19:23.200
I know you're building a strong case
against Tyrion.

282
00:19:23.360 --> 00:19:26.440
And as a mother. that is your right.

283
00:19:26.600 --> 00:19:30.560
But as a judge.
I cannot discuss the trial with you.

284
00:19:30.720 --> 00:19:32.880
I respect that.

285
00:19:35.560 --> 00:19:37.000
We don't need to discuss it.

286
00:19:40.240 --> 00:19:43.640
The Lannister legacy
is the only thing that matters.

287
00:19:43.800 --> 00:19:47.120
You've started wars
to protect this family.

288
00:19:47.280 --> 00:19:51.120
Turned your back on Jaime for
refusing to contribute to its future.

289
00:19:52.360 --> 00:19:54.560
What does Tyrion deserve

290
00:19:54.720 --> 00:19:57.080
for lighting that future on fire?

291
00:20:06.240 --> 00:20:08.480
ARYA: Joffrey.

292
00:20:08.640 --> 00:20:10.360
Cersei.

293
00:20:10.520 --> 00:20:12.720
Walder Frey.

294
00:20:12.880 --> 00:20:14.400
Meryn Trant.

295
00:20:14.560 --> 00:20:17.160
Tywin Lannister.

296
00:20:17.320 --> 00:20:20.080
The Red Woman.

297
00:20:20.240 --> 00:20:22.800
Beric Dondarrion.

298
00:20:22.960 --> 00:20:25.080
Thoros of Myr.

299
00:20:25.240 --> 00:20:28.240
Ilyn Payne. The Mountain.

300
00:20:28.400 --> 00:20:30.720
Would you shut up?

301
00:20:30.880 --> 00:20:33.600
I can't sleep until I say the names.

302
00:20:33.760 --> 00:20:37.960
The names of every fucking person
in Westeros?

303
00:20:38.120 --> 00:20:41.000
Only the ones I'm going to kill.
(THE HOUND SCOFFS)

304
00:20:41.160 --> 00:20:44.120
Hate's as good a thing as any
to keep a person going.

305
00:20:44.280 --> 00:20:46.160
Better than most.

306
00:20:47.760 --> 00:20:50.400
We come across my brother.

307
00:20:50.560 --> 00:20:53.240
maybe we can both cross a name
off our list.

308
00:20:56.320 --> 00:20:58.800
If he were here right now.
what would you do?

309
00:21:06.520 --> 00:21:10.440
I'd tell him to shut the fuck up
so I can get some sleep.

310
00:21:14.000 --> 00:21:16.160
Go on. get it over with.

311
00:21:16.320 --> 00:21:18.320
your list of doomed men.

312
00:21:20.560 --> 00:21:22.840
I'm almost done.

313
00:21:23.000 --> 00:21:25.400
Only one name left.

314
00:21:25.560 --> 00:21:27.600
Go on.

315
00:21:27.760 --> 00:21:29.720
(ARYA SIGHS)

316
00:21:35.400 --> 00:21:37.080
The Hound.

317
00:21:43.800 --> 00:21:46.560
-Thank you.
-Your mother always had a sweet tooth.

318
00:21:46.720 --> 00:21:48.160
-Really?
-Oh. yes.

319
00:21:48.320 --> 00:21:51.200
At suppertime.
she would go straight for honey cakes.

320
00:21:51.360 --> 00:21:54.240
candied almonds. custard.
Anything sweet.

321
00:21:54.400 --> 00:21:58.480
Eventually. your grandfather had
to assign a septa to watch her at meals.

322
00:21:58.640 --> 00:22:01.000
Cat was the firstborn daughter
after all.

323
00:22:01.160 --> 00:22:02.480
It was important
that she remain desirable

324
00:22:02.640 --> 00:22:05.200
so Father could arrange
a good match for her

325
00:22:05.360 --> 00:22:07.560
and she was starting to get fat.

326
00:22:07.720 --> 00:22:11.360
My mother fat?

327
00:22:12.720 --> 00:22:14.280
She never let me have my pudding

328
00:22:14.440 --> 00:22:16.440
until I'd finished all my proper food.

329
00:22:16.600 --> 00:22:19.400
This is before she married your father
and moved to the North.

330
00:22:19.560 --> 00:22:23.680
By the time you were born.
your father's austerity had become hers.

331
00:22:23.840 --> 00:22:25.760
Marriage changes people.

332
00:22:28.240 --> 00:22:30.080
(GASPS)
I didn't mean for you to stop.

333
00:22:30.240 --> 00:22:32.480
Go on. enjoy them.

334
00:22:36.480 --> 00:22:40.320
-How do you like them?
-They're delicious.

335
00:22:43.040 --> 00:22:45.200
Where did you get the lemons?
You can't grow them up here.

336
00:22:45.360 --> 00:22:46.680
Oh. gods. no.

337
00:22:46.840 --> 00:22:49.960
Petyr had three crates brought
all the way from King's Landing.

338
00:22:50.120 --> 00:22:53.160
-He knew you liked lemon cakes.
-He's so kind.

339
00:22:53.320 --> 00:22:56.000
He really cares for you.

340
00:22:56.160 --> 00:22:57.920
Think where you'd be without him.

341
00:22:58.080 --> 00:23:00.320
In their clutches and tried for murder.

342
00:23:02.120 --> 00:23:04.280
Yes. I'm very lucky.

343
00:23:04.440 --> 00:23:05.760
He feels responsible for you.

344
00:23:05.920 --> 00:23:09.520
-Oh. I know he does. I'm so grateful.
-Why?

345
00:23:09.680 --> 00:23:11.840
Why does he feel responsible for you?

346
00:23:13.440 --> 00:23:16.360
Well. I'm half Tully.
He loved your family so much.

347
00:23:16.520 --> 00:23:19.040
Loved your mother.
That's what you wanted to say.

348
00:23:19.200 --> 00:23:20.520
He loves you. Aunt Lysa.
He's married to you.

349
00:23:20.680 --> 00:23:22.920
Your mother never loved him. Never.

350
00:23:23.080 --> 00:23:25.520
Cat always went straight
for the sweetest thing.

351
00:23:25.680 --> 00:23:28.480
The most obvious thing.
Your Uncle Brandon.

352
00:23:28.640 --> 00:23:31.640
Your handsome. arrogant.
cruel Uncle Brandon.

353
00:23:31.800 --> 00:23:33.880
He almost killed Petyr in a duel.

354
00:23:34.040 --> 00:23:35.920
And your mother loved him anyway.

355
00:23:36.080 --> 00:23:39.720
And now Petyr is risking his life
to save you.

356
00:23:39.880 --> 00:23:42.160
the daughter
of a woman who didn't love him

357
00:23:42.320 --> 00:23:45.320
no more than those whores
in his brothels.

358
00:23:45.480 --> 00:23:47.680
-Has he told you about them?
-No.

359
00:23:47.840 --> 00:23:50.400
He hasn't told you about the vile
things they do with their bodies?

360
00:23:50.560 --> 00:23:52.600
The vile things they let him do
with their bodies?

361
00:23:52.760 --> 00:23:56.280
-No. never.
-Are you pregnant?

362
00:23:56.440 --> 00:23:58.880
What? No. I told you.
Lord Tyrion and I never--

363
00:23:59.040 --> 00:24:01.000
I wasn't asking about Tyrion.

364
00:24:01.160 --> 00:24:02.840
What have you let Petyr do
with your body?

365
00:24:03.000 --> 00:24:05.480
-Aunt Lysa. no. I--
-Your young. pretty body.

366
00:24:05.640 --> 00:24:08.320
-Nothing. I'm a virgin.
-Don't lie to me.

367
00:24:08.480 --> 00:24:11.200
You're hurting me.

368
00:24:11.360 --> 00:24:13.560
I'll know if you lie.

369
00:24:13.720 --> 00:24:17.000
I'm a virgin. I swear it.
He loves you. Aunt Lysa.

370
00:24:17.160 --> 00:24:18.920
All he says is that I'm stupid.

371
00:24:19.080 --> 00:24:20.800
I'm a stupid little girl
with stupid dreams

372
00:24:20.960 --> 00:24:22.800
who never learns
and I'm a terrible liar.

373
00:24:22.960 --> 00:24:25.000
so I should always tell the truth.
And I swear to you

374
00:24:25.160 --> 00:24:27.320
that he has never touched me.
Not once. not ever.

375
00:24:27.480 --> 00:24:30.200
Shh. Shh. Shh.

376
00:24:30.360 --> 00:24:33.960
It's all right.
It will all be all right.

377
00:24:34.120 --> 00:24:35.520
You'll be a widow soon.

378
00:24:35.680 --> 00:24:37.800
They'll execute that dwarf
for murdering the king

379
00:24:37.960 --> 00:24:40.000
and you'll be free to marry Robin.

380
00:24:40.160 --> 00:24:43.000
You'll be the Lady of the Vale. Hmm?

381
00:24:43.160 --> 00:24:46.840
(SANSA SIGHS)

382
00:24:50.400 --> 00:24:52.800
(HORSE WHINNIES)

383
00:24:57.280 --> 00:24:59.880
(GRUNTING)

384
00:25:05.680 --> 00:25:07.760
Didn't they teach you
how to ride a horse?

385
00:25:07.920 --> 00:25:10.560
Yes. my lady. when I was young.

386
00:25:10.720 --> 00:25:13.040
There wasn't much call for it
with Lord Tyrion. though.

387
00:25:14.320 --> 00:25:15.640
He preferred litters.

388
00:25:15.800 --> 00:25:18.240
Perhaps you should have stayed with him.

389
00:25:24.360 --> 00:25:26.200
It's not going to be
a pleasant journey for you.

390
00:25:26.360 --> 00:25:29.720
It could take weeks to get to the Wall.
depending on the weather.

391
00:25:29.880 --> 00:25:31.200
That's a long way off.

392
00:25:31.360 --> 00:25:34.360
Well. Lady Sansa's brother's
at Castle Black.

393
00:25:34.520 --> 00:25:37.360
If I were her. that's where I'd go.

394
00:25:37.520 --> 00:25:39.000
Feel free to stop at any point.

395
00:25:39.160 --> 00:25:41.840
Never. my lady. I'm your squire.

396
00:25:42.000 --> 00:25:44.320
I've made it this far in the world
without a squire.

397
00:25:44.480 --> 00:25:47.400
-I don't see why I need one now.
-All knights have squires. my lady.

398
00:25:47.560 --> 00:25:51.680
I'm not a knight. And I'm not a slaver.
either. I don't own you.

399
00:25:51.840 --> 00:25:54.120
I swore an oath. my lady.

400
00:25:54.280 --> 00:25:56.080
I am releasing you from that oath.

401
00:25:59.560 --> 00:26:01.200
That means you could leave.

402
00:26:01.360 --> 00:26:03.520
I know.

403
00:26:03.680 --> 00:26:05.840
What do you think will happen
if you leave?

404
00:26:07.160 --> 00:26:09.000
They'll say I wasn't a very good squire.

405
00:26:09.160 --> 00:26:14.240
(HORSE NICKERS. WHINNIES)

406
00:27:01.720 --> 00:27:04.760
-The hell you doing?
-Practicing.

407
00:27:04.920 --> 00:27:07.600
-What. ways to die?
-No one's going to kill me.

408
00:27:07.760 --> 00:27:10.440
They will if you nance around like that.

409
00:27:10.600 --> 00:27:12.040
That's no way to fight.

410
00:27:12.200 --> 00:27:14.880
It's not fighting. It's water dancing.

411
00:27:15.040 --> 00:27:16.840
Dancing?

412
00:27:17.000 --> 00:27:19.240
Maybe you ought to put on a dress.

413
00:27:21.000 --> 00:27:23.160
Who taught you that shite?

414
00:27:23.320 --> 00:27:25.080
The greatest swordsman who ever lived.

415
00:27:27.920 --> 00:27:30.960
Syrio Forel. the First Sword
to the Sealord of Braavos.

416
00:27:31.120 --> 00:27:34.080
Braavos.
Greasy-haired little bastard. I bet.

417
00:27:34.240 --> 00:27:36.800
-They all are.
-What do you know about anything?

418
00:27:36.960 --> 00:27:39.000
I bet his hair is greasier
than Joffrey's cunt.

419
00:27:39.160 --> 00:27:40.960
-It was not.
-Was? He dead?

420
00:27:41.120 --> 00:27:42.880
Yes. He was killed.

421
00:27:43.040 --> 00:27:45.360
-Who by?
-Meryn Trant. That's why Ser Meryn--

422
00:27:45.520 --> 00:27:47.000
Meryn Trant?

423
00:27:47.160 --> 00:27:50.160
The greatest swordsman who ever lived
killed by Meryn fucking Trant?

424
00:27:50.320 --> 00:27:52.040
-He was outnumbered.
-Any boy whore with a sword

425
00:27:52.200 --> 00:27:53.920
could beat three Meryn Trants.

426
00:27:54.080 --> 00:27:56.480
Syrio didn't have a sword.
Or armor. Just a stick.

427
00:27:56.640 --> 00:27:59.040
The greatest swordsman who ever lived
didn't have a sword?

428
00:27:59.200 --> 00:28:00.640
(LAUGHS)

429
00:28:00.800 --> 00:28:04.160
All right. You have a sword.
Let's see what he taught you.

430
00:28:04.320 --> 00:28:07.760
Go on. do it for your Braavosi friend.

431
00:28:07.920 --> 00:28:11.200
Dead like all the rest of your friends.

432
00:28:11.360 --> 00:28:13.160
(GRUNTS)

433
00:28:21.040 --> 00:28:24.160
Your friend's dead and Meryn Trant's not

434
00:28:24.320 --> 00:28:26.080
'cause Trant had armor

435
00:28:26.240 --> 00:28:28.440
and a big fucking sword.

436
00:28:31.520 --> 00:28:34.360
(PANTING)

437
00:28:41.040 --> 00:28:44.120
(BIRD CALLING)

438
00:28:57.560 --> 00:28:58.880
Your Grace.

439
00:28:59.040 --> 00:29:02.360
Prince Oberyn. Writing letters?

440
00:29:02.520 --> 00:29:05.440
A poem. actually.

441
00:29:05.600 --> 00:29:07.440
May I show you the gardens?

442
00:29:07.600 --> 00:29:10.360
I couldn't very well refuse
a royal escort.

443
00:29:10.520 --> 00:29:12.320
No. you couldn't.

444
00:29:14.320 --> 00:29:16.840
I didn't realize you were a poet.

445
00:29:17.000 --> 00:29:19.360
Not a very good one.
(CERSEI CHUCKLES)

446
00:29:19.520 --> 00:29:21.840
For your paramour?

447
00:29:22.000 --> 00:29:23.760
For one of my daughters.

448
00:29:23.920 --> 00:29:26.360
You have several. don't you?

449
00:29:26.520 --> 00:29:29.200
-Eight.
-Eight?

450
00:29:29.360 --> 00:29:30.920
Eight daughters?

451
00:29:31.080 --> 00:29:32.960
The fifth is difficult.

452
00:29:33.120 --> 00:29:35.520
I named her after my sister. Elia.

453
00:29:35.680 --> 00:29:37.400
Beautiful name.

454
00:29:37.560 --> 00:29:39.160
Yes.

455
00:29:39.320 --> 00:29:42.640
But I can't say it without turning sad.

456
00:29:42.800 --> 00:29:44.760
And after I turn sad.

457
00:29:44.920 --> 00:29:46.880
I grow angry.

458
00:29:47.040 --> 00:29:50.200
Perhaps that's why she's difficult.

459
00:29:50.360 --> 00:29:52.400
The gods love their stupid jokes.
don't they?

460
00:29:52.560 --> 00:29:55.200
Which joke is that?

461
00:29:55.360 --> 00:29:57.360
You're a prince of Dorne.

462
00:29:57.520 --> 00:29:58.880
A legendary fighter.

463
00:29:59.040 --> 00:30:01.960
A brilliant man
feared throughout Westeros.

464
00:30:02.120 --> 00:30:04.200
But you could not save your sister.

465
00:30:04.360 --> 00:30:07.200
I'm a Lannister. Queen for 19 years.

466
00:30:07.360 --> 00:30:10.400
Daughter of the most powerful man alive.

467
00:30:10.560 --> 00:30:13.320
But I could not save my son.

468
00:30:13.480 --> 00:30:15.280
What good is power

469
00:30:15.440 --> 00:30:17.440
if you cannot protect the ones you love?

470
00:30:17.600 --> 00:30:19.040
We can avenge them.

471
00:30:19.200 --> 00:30:22.360
Yes. we can avenge them.

472
00:30:22.520 --> 00:30:26.960
You really believe
Tyrion murdered your son?

473
00:30:27.120 --> 00:30:28.880
I know he did.

474
00:30:30.600 --> 00:30:33.720
We will have a trial
and we will learn the truth.

475
00:30:33.880 --> 00:30:36.240
We'll have a trial. anyway.

476
00:30:40.080 --> 00:30:42.600
I haven't seen my daughter
in over a year.

477
00:30:42.760 --> 00:30:44.800
The last time I saw her.

478
00:30:44.960 --> 00:30:47.800
she was swimming with two
of my girls in the Water Gardens.

479
00:30:47.960 --> 00:30:50.960
(CHUCKLES)
Laughing in the sun.

480
00:30:52.600 --> 00:30:55.400
I want to believe that.

481
00:30:55.560 --> 00:30:57.160
I want to believe she's happy.

482
00:30:57.320 --> 00:30:59.080
You have my word.

483
00:31:00.320 --> 00:31:02.280
We don't hurt little girls in Dorne.

484
00:31:04.120 --> 00:31:07.000
Everywhere in the world.
they hurt little girls.

485
00:31:16.120 --> 00:31:18.280
Would you bring her a gift for me?

486
00:31:19.400 --> 00:31:21.000
I wasn't there for her name day.

487
00:31:21.160 --> 00:31:23.200
I don't know when I'll see her again.

488
00:31:23.360 --> 00:31:26.040
Anything at all.

489
00:31:27.080 --> 00:31:28.720
The best shipwrights in King's Landing

490
00:31:28.880 --> 00:31:30.800
have been working on it for months.

491
00:31:31.960 --> 00:31:34.240
Myrcella loves the open water.

492
00:31:34.400 --> 00:31:38.000
OBERYN: I will have it sailed
down to Sunspear for her.

493
00:31:39.760 --> 00:31:41.560
Please tell her...

494
00:31:43.840 --> 00:31:46.040
...her mother misses her very much.

495
00:31:54.480 --> 00:31:57.840
PODRICK: Oh. no. no. no.

496
00:31:59.640 --> 00:32:01.280
Hells.

497
00:32:04.960 --> 00:32:06.640
Gods.
(SIGHS)

498
00:32:09.440 --> 00:32:10.760
Did you remove the skin?

499
00:32:13.240 --> 00:32:14.560
No. my lady.

500
00:32:14.720 --> 00:32:16.280
Have you ever cooked a rabbit before?

501
00:32:17.840 --> 00:32:19.840
No. my lady.

502
00:32:20.000 --> 00:32:22.240
Did you ever cook anything
for Lord Tyrion?

503
00:32:22.400 --> 00:32:24.120
No. my lady.

504
00:32:25.560 --> 00:32:27.840
That was the cooks.

505
00:32:28.000 --> 00:32:29.360
(GROANS)

506
00:32:43.800 --> 00:32:47.040
-What are you doing?
-I'm helping you with your armor.

507
00:32:47.200 --> 00:32:49.920
I've been removing my own armor for
quite some time. thank you very much.

508
00:33:07.360 --> 00:33:09.920
What exactly did you do for Lord Tyrion?

509
00:33:10.080 --> 00:33:13.120
I brought him his meals and cleared
his table when he was finished.

510
00:33:13.280 --> 00:33:15.640
I kept his clothing and linens clean.

511
00:33:15.800 --> 00:33:18.000
Carried his messages
and returned the replies.

512
00:33:20.280 --> 00:33:23.760
-Mostly I poured wine.
-Oh.

513
00:33:23.920 --> 00:33:25.320
Whilst in Lord Tyrion's service.

514
00:33:25.480 --> 00:33:28.400
did you ever do anything
remotely related to combat?

515
00:33:32.640 --> 00:33:34.480
I killed a man.

516
00:33:37.640 --> 00:33:39.800
Who?

517
00:33:39.960 --> 00:33:41.680
A Kingsguard.

518
00:33:45.840 --> 00:33:48.640
He tried to kill Lord Tyrion
at the Blackwater.

519
00:33:52.520 --> 00:33:54.480
How did you kill a Kingsguard?

520
00:33:56.440 --> 00:33:59.520
I pushed a spear
through the back of his head.

521
00:34:10.360 --> 00:34:12.320
Bloody ridiculous.

522
00:34:16.080 --> 00:34:17.680
Help me with these straps.

523
00:34:27.640 --> 00:34:30.960
(WOMAN WHIMPERING. RAST LAUGHING)

524
00:34:36.040 --> 00:34:40.360
RAST: Hey. Hey. get up.

525
00:34:40.520 --> 00:34:43.000
Get up.
(WOMAN SOBBING)

526
00:34:48.800 --> 00:34:50.800
MAN: That's it lad. put it inside.

527
00:34:50.960 --> 00:34:52.720
Get the fire going again.
We're all freezing.

528
00:34:52.880 --> 00:34:54.920
Aye. What we need is a girl there.

529
00:34:55.080 --> 00:34:57.200
I've got to have a piss.

530
00:35:03.480 --> 00:35:05.800
(PIGS GRUNTING)

531
00:35:05.960 --> 00:35:08.320
(WOMEN WHIMPERING)

532
00:35:09.360 --> 00:35:11.400
Now keep quiet.

533
00:35:21.200 --> 00:35:23.280
(LANTERN RATTLES)

534
00:35:34.640 --> 00:35:37.440
(LANTERN SQUEAKING)

535
00:35:47.600 --> 00:35:50.760
(COUGHS)

536
00:35:50.920 --> 00:35:53.280
You need water.

537
00:35:53.440 --> 00:35:54.800
It doesn't matter.

538
00:35:54.960 --> 00:35:56.920
Of course it matters.

539
00:36:00.240 --> 00:36:01.960
You mustn't let anything stop you.

540
00:36:04.440 --> 00:36:07.040
They already have stopped me.

541
00:36:07.200 --> 00:36:09.040
No.

542
00:36:11.640 --> 00:36:13.320
You're not here.

543
00:36:19.120 --> 00:36:21.040
You're far from here.

544
00:36:23.360 --> 00:36:25.280
What does that mean?

545
00:36:25.440 --> 00:36:27.960
(CROWS CAWING)

546
00:36:31.000 --> 00:36:32.840
At the hill.

547
00:36:33.840 --> 00:36:35.600
A great weirwood tree.

548
00:36:37.040 --> 00:36:39.880
You've seen it. too.

549
00:36:40.040 --> 00:36:43.400
Meera and I. even Hodor.

550
00:36:44.800 --> 00:36:46.680
we're only here to guide you.

551
00:36:48.560 --> 00:36:50.320
(CROW CAWING)

552
00:36:50.480 --> 00:36:52.280
He's waiting for you.

553
00:36:54.400 --> 00:36:56.000
We have to find it.

554
00:36:57.600 --> 00:37:00.240
You have to make it.

555
00:37:00.400 --> 00:37:02.760
We will.

556
00:37:02.920 --> 00:37:06.160
This-- this isn't the end.

557
00:37:07.600 --> 00:37:10.160
Not for you.

558
00:37:10.320 --> 00:37:12.080
Not yet.

559
00:37:12.240 --> 00:37:13.920
MEERA: How...

560
00:37:14.080 --> 00:37:16.360
will we know the end?

561
00:37:28.280 --> 00:37:29.920
You'll know.

562
00:37:32.840 --> 00:37:35.760
(FOOTSTEPS)

563
00:37:42.280 --> 00:37:44.120
LOCKE: Brothers.

564
00:37:45.440 --> 00:37:47.480
You do move quiet.

565
00:37:49.400 --> 00:37:51.240
-How many?
-11 men.

566
00:37:51.400 --> 00:37:53.040
Most of them already drunk.

567
00:37:53.200 --> 00:37:56.600
No guards posted. They don't seem
to have a care in the world.

568
00:37:56.760 --> 00:37:59.560
We'll carve them up like walnut pie.

569
00:37:59.720 --> 00:38:02.640
Karl was a top paid cutthroat
in Flea Bottom.

570
00:38:02.800 --> 00:38:04.120
I've seen what he can do with a knife.

571
00:38:04.280 --> 00:38:07.400
Have you seen what I can do
with a knife?

572
00:38:07.560 --> 00:38:09.280
Not yet.

573
00:38:10.880 --> 00:38:12.520
There's a hut
on the west side of the keep.

574
00:38:12.680 --> 00:38:15.160
-We should steer clear of it.
-Why?

575
00:38:15.320 --> 00:38:18.560
They've got some hounds
chained up inside.

576
00:38:18.720 --> 00:38:22.560
Closer we can get without the dogs
sniffing us. the better.

577
00:38:22.720 --> 00:38:24.680
New moon tonight.

578
00:38:27.040 --> 00:38:30.000
(SIGHS)
Get some rest.

579
00:38:30.160 --> 00:38:31.560
We move at sundown.

580
00:38:33.760 --> 00:38:35.920
I've always liked a girl with curls.

581
00:38:36.080 --> 00:38:37.800
A touch of class.

582
00:38:37.960 --> 00:38:40.040
You take whatever's left.

583
00:38:43.640 --> 00:38:45.000
Get her up.

584
00:38:46.440 --> 00:38:48.960
BRAN: Stop. Stop.
What are you doing?

585
00:38:49.120 --> 00:38:51.640
HODOR: Hodor. Hodor. Hodor.

586
00:38:51.800 --> 00:38:54.600
Stop. Stop!

587
00:38:54.760 --> 00:38:57.680
-HODOR: Hodor. Hodor.
-BRAN: Stop!

588
00:38:58.800 --> 00:39:01.080
-Please.
-Hodor.

589
00:39:01.240 --> 00:39:04.000
-Please. get off her!
-Hodor. Hodor.

590
00:39:04.160 --> 00:39:06.280
Please! Please. leave her alone!

591
00:39:09.320 --> 00:39:11.920
BRAN: Please. stop. Stop.

592
00:39:12.080 --> 00:39:14.400
-What are you doing? Leave her alone!
-Hodor. Hodor.

593
00:39:14.560 --> 00:39:16.680
-No!
-Shh.

594
00:39:16.840 --> 00:39:18.760
(GASPING)

595
00:39:18.920 --> 00:39:22.440
-Shh.
(WHIMPERING)

596
00:39:25.520 --> 00:39:27.040
You've got pretty hair. don't you?

597
00:39:29.160 --> 00:39:31.760
Now what is a pretty
little highborn girl like you

598
00:39:31.920 --> 00:39:35.120
doing out here
in the deep. dark woods. eh?

599
00:39:36.520 --> 00:39:40.040
You left your daddy's castle
looking for trouble. didn't you?

600
00:39:40.200 --> 00:39:42.240
No dresses for you.

601
00:39:43.720 --> 00:39:46.360
You like it rough. don't you?

602
00:39:46.520 --> 00:39:49.520
You like it in the gutter. don't you?

603
00:39:49.680 --> 00:39:52.240
If you let my sister go. I can help you.

604
00:39:53.640 --> 00:39:55.320
You can help me?

605
00:39:55.480 --> 00:39:57.000
I can.

606
00:39:59.080 --> 00:40:00.800
And how you gonna do that?

607
00:40:04.360 --> 00:40:07.360
I have the sight. I can see things.

608
00:40:07.520 --> 00:40:09.360
That's very helpful.

609
00:40:09.520 --> 00:40:11.280
Things that haven't happened yet.

610
00:40:15.560 --> 00:40:17.400
What a fine thing.

611
00:40:20.560 --> 00:40:22.720
A fine thing.

612
00:40:23.920 --> 00:40:26.760
Have you seen what I'm gonna do
to your sister?

613
00:40:29.200 --> 00:40:32.920
Have you seen what they're going to do
to your sister?

614
00:40:34.880 --> 00:40:36.640
No.

615
00:40:38.960 --> 00:40:41.400
Don't close your eyes.

616
00:40:46.600 --> 00:40:48.840
I saw you die tonight.

617
00:40:50.680 --> 00:40:53.000
I saw your body burn.

618
00:40:53.160 --> 00:40:57.120
I saw the snow fall and bury your bones.

619
00:41:00.320 --> 00:41:02.760
MAN: To arms!

620
00:41:02.920 --> 00:41:05.480
They're here. the Night's Watch.

621
00:41:05.640 --> 00:41:08.120
(MEN SHOUTING)

622
00:41:12.880 --> 00:41:15.200
(WOMAN SCREAMING)

623
00:41:17.320 --> 00:41:19.000
(GRUNTING)

624
00:41:28.480 --> 00:41:30.560
(SCREAMS)

625
00:41:33.600 --> 00:41:37.160
Rescue party is here. lads. Lady.

626
00:41:37.320 --> 00:41:39.720
-Is Jon with you?
-Aye.

627
00:41:39.880 --> 00:41:42.800
I'll take you to him.

628
00:41:45.040 --> 00:41:47.440
You're Brandon Stark?

629
00:41:52.000 --> 00:41:53.600
(GASPS)
Hodor. Hodor.

630
00:41:53.760 --> 00:41:56.240
The little crippled lord.
We're going for a ride. boy.

631
00:41:56.400 --> 00:41:57.880
Jon! Jon!

632
00:41:58.040 --> 00:42:01.160
Keep talking
and I'll cut your friends' throats.

633
00:42:02.280 --> 00:42:05.720
Starting with the idiot. Do you hear?

634
00:42:05.880 --> 00:42:08.600
Do you hear?

635
00:42:19.360 --> 00:42:21.320
HODOR: Hodor! Hodor!

636
00:42:22.640 --> 00:42:24.640
Hodor. Hodor.

637
00:42:24.800 --> 00:42:27.320
Hodor. Hodor.

638
00:42:29.280 --> 00:42:32.240
Hodor. Hodor. Hodor.

639
00:42:36.840 --> 00:42:41.360
(HEAVY BREATHING. GRUNTING)

640
00:43:01.760 --> 00:43:04.840
(CHOKING)

641
00:43:07.640 --> 00:43:09.600
(NECK CRACKS)

642
00:43:12.640 --> 00:43:14.440
Hodor.

643
00:43:15.800 --> 00:43:20.120
BRAN: Hodor. get his knife.
Cut me loose.

644
00:43:20.280 --> 00:43:24.640
-BRAN: Hodor. get his knife.
-Hodor.

645
00:43:24.800 --> 00:43:27.160
Cut me loose. Hodor.

646
00:43:32.520 --> 00:43:35.320
Jojen and Meera. free them.

647
00:43:35.480 --> 00:43:37.480
Go!

648
00:43:37.640 --> 00:43:40.440
(SWORDS CLANKING. MEN SHOUTING)

649
00:43:40.600 --> 00:43:42.480
Jon.

650
00:43:51.400 --> 00:43:53.920
Jon!

651
00:43:54.080 --> 00:43:56.040
If he sees you.
he won't let you go north.

652
00:43:56.200 --> 00:43:58.920
-He's my brother.
-And wants to protect you.

653
00:43:59.080 --> 00:44:01.560
He'll take you back to Castle Black.

654
00:44:03.160 --> 00:44:05.080
You have to decide.

655
00:44:05.240 --> 00:44:06.960
Do you want to find
the three-eyed raven?

656
00:44:20.960 --> 00:44:23.400
-BRAN: Hodor.
-HODOR: Hodor.

657
00:44:23.560 --> 00:44:25.800
We need to free Summer.

658
00:44:25.960 --> 00:44:27.760
And we need to go.

659
00:44:32.440 --> 00:44:34.840
(SHOUTS. MAN GROANS)

660
00:44:41.920 --> 00:44:44.080
Lord Snow.

661
00:44:44.240 --> 00:44:46.400
Are you bringing me back for trial?

662
00:44:48.600 --> 00:44:50.720
We had a good thing here.

663
00:44:50.880 --> 00:44:53.200
We were free men.

664
00:44:53.360 --> 00:44:55.400
You'll never be free.

665
00:44:55.560 --> 00:44:57.840
You'll never know what that's like.

666
00:45:17.760 --> 00:45:20.480
You learn how to fight in a castle?

667
00:45:23.240 --> 00:45:25.360
(GROANS)

668
00:45:25.520 --> 00:45:28.960
Some old man teach you how to stand.
how to parry?

669
00:45:29.120 --> 00:45:30.560
(GROANS)

670
00:45:32.720 --> 00:45:34.840
How to fight with honor?

671
00:45:47.480 --> 00:45:49.520
You know what's wrong with honor?

672
00:45:49.680 --> 00:45:51.560
(SPITS)

673
00:45:55.200 --> 00:45:57.160
(GRUNTS)

674
00:45:59.840 --> 00:46:02.240
You.

675
00:46:10.440 --> 00:46:12.320
(GURGLING)

676
00:46:21.600 --> 00:46:24.120
(PANTING)

677
00:46:31.800 --> 00:46:33.640
Are you all right?

678
00:46:36.280 --> 00:46:38.760
Come with me.

679
00:46:38.920 --> 00:46:40.800
Come on.

680
00:46:44.560 --> 00:46:47.120
(GRUNTS)

681
00:46:56.600 --> 00:46:59.240
We lost four brothers?

682
00:46:59.400 --> 00:47:01.360
Five.

683
00:47:03.840 --> 00:47:06.440
What the seven hells could do that
to a man?

684
00:47:08.440 --> 00:47:11.360
I count 10 dead mutineers.

685
00:47:11.520 --> 00:47:13.640
Locke said there were 11 of them.

686
00:47:14.760 --> 00:47:16.080
Where's Rast?

687
00:47:16.240 --> 00:47:18.760
(WIND HOWLING)

688
00:47:21.680 --> 00:47:24.480
(PANTING)

689
00:47:37.120 --> 00:47:39.520
(CROWS CAWING)

690
00:47:50.920 --> 00:47:53.240
(ROARING. RAST SCREAMS)

691
00:47:58.560 --> 00:48:00.600
-Here's another.
-Jon.

692
00:48:03.920 --> 00:48:06.880
JON: Where in seven hells?

693
00:48:07.040 --> 00:48:09.160
Come here.

694
00:48:11.520 --> 00:48:14.640
(DIREWOLF WHINING)

695
00:48:14.800 --> 00:48:18.160
I missed you. boy.

696
00:48:21.000 --> 00:48:22.560
What should we do with this lot?

697
00:48:27.760 --> 00:48:30.160
It's not safe for you here on your own.

698
00:48:30.320 --> 00:48:31.960
Mance Rayder has an army
heading this way

699
00:48:32.120 --> 00:48:34.360
and there's worse out there than Mance.

700
00:48:36.840 --> 00:48:39.720
Come with us to Castle Black.

701
00:48:39.880 --> 00:48:42.240
We can find you work. Keep you safe.

702
00:48:42.400 --> 00:48:44.840
Meaning all respect. Ser Crow.

703
00:48:45.000 --> 00:48:48.640
Craster beat us and worse.

704
00:48:48.800 --> 00:48:51.080
Your brother crows beat us and worse.

705
00:48:51.240 --> 00:48:53.040
We'll find our own way.

706
00:48:53.200 --> 00:48:55.480
You want to stay here

707
00:48:55.640 --> 00:48:57.800
in Craster's Keep?

708
00:48:59.960 --> 00:49:03.120
(SPITS)
Burn it to the ground

709
00:49:03.280 --> 00:49:05.520
and all the dead with it.
